WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.540
At Mount Sinai, the Torah describes
the voice of a horn, exceeding loud.

2
00:00:05.590 --> 00:00:08.630
When Solomon is made
king, a horn is blown.

3
00:00:08.680 --> 00:00:13.080
Every autumn, the Torah says,
comes a day of blowing the horn.

4
00:00:13.130 --> 00:00:18.800
Ten days later, many Jews go without
food or water for about 25 hours.

5
00:00:18.850 --> 00:00:24.190
So why blow a ram's horn, then
fast for 25 hours ten days later?

6
00:00:24.240 --> 00:00:27.950
In this mission, you'll trace the
horn through the Hebrew scriptures.

7
00:00:28.000 --> 00:00:32.680
Then you'll follow Yom Kippur from its
first evening to the closing of the gates.

8
00:00:32.730 --> 00:00:36.270
Your mission: find out why
Jews blow a ram's horn,

9
00:00:36.320 --> 00:00:39.310
then fast for 25 hours ten days later.
